{"seq":15,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T17:03:15.163Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"ff1786c9bb4a647cdeb6d2c893114a45485a59485f116f6b1693386284f2501e","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers I found in Moss's notes:\n\n- **#PD-4492**: Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk alerts, where drivers at Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Thea submitted it on 4 Oct 2025, and support patched it that evening. Source: `teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md` (\"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\", 5 Oct 2025).\n- **#4419**: gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. Thea logged it, and it was later escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. Source: `teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md` (\"Moss: North cheat sheet\", undated).\n\nMoss's other North digests (14 Sep 2025 pipeline, 23 Mar 2026 renewals) don't carry a QFL ticket number. The Central handoffs digest has #4409 and #4412, but those belong to Pree's dealer account, not QFL, so I left them out.\n\nFor the weekly notes, be aware that the 28 May 2025 handoff email from Ilse also cites #4419, but for the Duluth Gate 3 kiosk glitch. That email isn't one of Moss's notes, so I didn't count it, but the number's description differs from the cheat sheet's, so you may want to check it against the ticket system before you cite it."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
